## Reviewer Report

### 🟠 Major (strongly recommended)
- `scripts/ladder-run.sh:106` — Same bug class the release claims to have eradicated ("the REAL empty_output root cause: pipefail + grep -q", `CHANGELOG.md:27`) survives unaudited here. The file sets `set -euo pipefail` (`scripts/ladder-run.sh:2`) and does `printf '%s\n' "$report" | grep -q 'OVERALL escape rate'` where `$report` is the full `qc_metric.py report` output. Under `pipefail`, if `grep -q` finds the pattern early and exits before `printf` finishes writing a sufficiently large `$report` (once it exceeds the OS pipe buffer, ~64KB on Linux), `printf` SIGPIPEs and the pipeline's exit status becomes non-zero even though the pattern *was* found — this is structurally identical to the just-fixed `dispatch-author.sh` bug (grep exits fast on a large piped payload, upstream writer gets SIGPIPE under pipefail). Consequence here: `CALC_OK` silently drops to 0 and `promotion_decision` fail-closes (`scripts/ladder-run.sh:107-108`, `:122`) — the acceptance-ladder promotion recommendation goes dark for large QC stores with no error surfaced, exactly the "small outputs pass, is why every probe kept lying" masking pattern called out in the CHANGELOG for the original bug. Two other pre-existing occurrences in the codebase (`scripts/check-disjointness.sh:67`, `scripts/dispatch-batch.sh:71`) already carry an explicit comment warning about this exact anti-pattern and route around it — `ladder-run.sh:106` has no such guard. Fix: apply the same `grep -c '...' > /dev/null` treatment used in this commit's own fix, or switch to pure-bash matching (`[[ "$report" == *"OVERALL escape rate"* ]]`) which needs no subshell pipe at all. Given the commit's own headline claims root-cause closure for this bug class, this is a completeness gap on the claim, not a new-diff regression — but it belongs in this release's scope per the "claimed but missing" decomposition (the implied outcome "pipefail+grep -q epidemic eradicated" is not fully delivered while a structurally identical instance remains).

