### ✅ Verified Clean
- `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:215-219` / `platforms/codex/plugin/scripts/dispatch-author.sh:215-219` — the actual fix. Confirmed `set -uo pipefail` is active (`scripts/dispatch-author.sh:48`); confirmed `grep -c PATTERN > /dev/null` reads to EOF (no early-exit optimization, unlike `-q`/`-l`) so `tr`/`sed` never receive SIGPIPE; confirmed the `if !` exit-code semantics are preserved (grep -c still exits 0 on ≥1 matching line, 1 on none), so the empty/non-empty classification logic is unchanged in outcome, only in the code path that avoids the pipefail false-negative. Confirmed the two mirrors (`scripts/` canonical and `platforms/codex/plugin/scripts/` payload) received byte-identical hunks.
- `hooks/tests/dispatch-output-quiescence.test.sh:126-135` — new regression test genuinely exercises the fixed defect class: `head -c 6000 /dev/urandom | base64` produces a multi-KB non-whitespace payload (the size class the CHANGELOG measured 97/100 false-empty on), asserts exit 0 / status `authored` / elapsed ≤ 6s. Traced `wait_output_quiescent` (`scripts/lib/output-quiescence.sh:33-77`) confirming its default stability window (`stable_polls=4` × 250ms ≈ 1s) makes the 6s bound realistic and consistent with the pre-existing `immediate-content` test's 5s bound — not a flaky assertion. `make_stub`/`run_dispatch`/`assert_le` are pre-existing helpers (lines 13-84 of the file, untouched by this diff), correctly reused.
