### Summary
Overall risk: Low
Top 3 priorities to fix:
1. 🟠 `scripts/ladder-run.sh:106` — apply the same `grep -c … > /dev/null` (or pure-bash `[[ … == *pattern* ]]`) fix to close the identical pipefail+grep-q hole in the QC-ladder promotion-decision path; the release's "root cause eradicated" claim isn't fully true while this survives.
2. 🟡 Add a one-line CHANGELOG disclosure covering the 3 mechanical mirror-sync files bundled in via the concurrent-session rebase (`.opencode/agent-bodies/reviewer.body.md`, `platforms/codex/plugin/skills/finish-flow/SKILL.md`, `platforms/codex/plugin/scripts/preflight-release.sh`).
3. (Optional, low-cost) grep the rest of the repo (not just `scripts/`) for the `cmd | grep -q` + `pipefail` pattern as a one-time sweep, since two instances (`check-disjointness.sh`, `dispatch-batch.sh`) already needed hand-written warnings to avoid it — a `completeness-scan.sh`-style regex gate for this anti-pattern would prevent recurrence better than case-by-case fixes.

### Handoff
Next consumer: MAIN_CLAUDE
Routing rationale: The Major finding (`ladder-run.sh:106`) has a clear, mechanical fix identical in shape to the one already applied in this diff — no root-cause investigation or domain specialist needed.
Remaining risks: `ladder-run.sh:106`'s exposure is probabilistic (only manifests once `$report` exceeds the OS pipe buffer, i.e. once the QC store accumulates enough samples) — low likelihood today, growing over time as the ladder harness accumulates events; failure mode is fail-closed (never promotes) rather than fail-open, so no immediate safety risk, but it will eventually reproduce the same "silently lying gate" class this release exists to close.
